  "decision": "Refused",
  "postcode": "KT1 1HN",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal would result in the unjustified loss of existing commercial moorings with no robust marketing evidence or viability assessment to demonstrate that continued employment, leisure, or tourism uses are unviable, contrary to Policy DM17 of the Kingston Core Strategy (2012) and Policies SI16 and SI17 of the London Plan (2021).",
    "The change of use would reduce capacity for waterborne passenger and tourist traffic, conflicting with the strategic objectives of the Blue Ribbon Network and Thames Policy Area contrary to Policy DM7 of the Core Strategy and Policies SI15-SI17 of the London Plan (2021).",
    "The site is located in Flood Zone 3b (Functional Floodplain), where 'more vulnerable' development, including permanent residential accommodation, is not permitted, contrary to the Policy SI 12 of the London Plan 2021 and Policy DM4 of the Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The proposed permanent residential moorings would detract from the character and visual quality of the riverside setting within the Riverside South and Kingston Town Conservation Areas and would result in less than substantial harm to the significance of the designated heritage asset and the setting of nearby listed buildings. In the absence of any identified public benefits to outweigh this harm, the proposal conflicts with Paragraphs 215 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3 and HC1 of the London Plan (2021), Policy DM12 of Kingston's Core Strategy (2012).",
    "Insufficient information has been provided regarding the height, design, and materials of the proposed houseboats. In the absence of this detail, it is not possible to undertake a comprehensive assessment of the proposal's impact on neighbouring amenity, contrary to Policy D3 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy DM10 of the Kingston Core Strategy (2012).",
    "Insufficient details, in the form of a detailed refuse and waste management plan, has been submitted to demonstrate how waste storage and collection would be appropriately managed for the proposed development, contrary to Policy D6 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy DM10 of Kingston's Core Strategy (2012).",
    "Insufficient details on cycle storage has been submitted to demonstrate cycle parking could be provided to encourage future occupants to use sustainable modes of travel, contrary to Policy T5 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy DM10 of the Kingston Core Strategy (2012)."
  ],
